## Running the Python Analyzer

Make sure Python is installed.

Open a terminal inside the project folder and run:

```bash
python soc_analyzer.py
```

The analyzer will read `sample_logs.txt` and display the detected activity and security alerts in the terminal.

## Running the Dashboard

Because the dashboard loads `sample_logs.txt` using JavaScript, it should be opened through a local web server rather than directly through a `file://` URL.

One option is to use the Live Server extension in Visual Studio Code.

Open `index.html` and select:

```text
Open with Live Server
```

The SOC dashboard will then load in your browser and analyze the sample log data.

