One of the main things I learned from this project is that individual security events may not look particularly suspicious on their own. Looking at multiple related events together can reveal patterns that may require investigation.

## Limitations

This is an educational cybersecurity project and is not intended to replace a production SIEM or SOC monitoring platform.

The current detection rules are based on simple thresholds and synthetic authentication logs. A real security monitoring environment would require more advanced correlation, time-based detection, larger datasets, additional log sources, and methods for reducing false positives.

